select null, t.id, 'builtin', 'Rh immune globulin should be given to a D-negative mother who delivered a D-positive baby within:', '["24 hours","72 hours","7 days","28 days"]'::jsonb, 1, 'RhIG is given within 72 hours of delivery (with a routine dose at 26–28 weeks) to prevent anti-D. A standard 300 µg dose covers about 15 mL of fetal red cells; a Kleihauer-Betke test guides extra doses for larger bleeds. Reference: StatPearls, Rho(D) Immune Globulin (ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK557884) and Kleihauer-Betke Test (ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK430876).', '["Within the window, but not the outer limit.","Give as soon as possible, within 72 hours of delivery.","Too late for the standard dose window.","Antenatal dose is given at about 28 weeks, a different timing."]'::jsonb, 1, 'verified'
