select null, t.id, 'builtin', 'The Kleihauer-Betke test is used to:', '["Estimate the volume of fetomaternal hemorrhage","Determine the ABO group of the fetus","Detect weak D","Identify red cell antibodies"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The Kleihauer-Betke test estimates how much fetal blood entered the mother, which guides the RhIG dose. Reference: FIGO/ICM guidelines for preventing Rhesus disease: A call to action (pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7898700).', '["Acid elution removes adult Hb; fetal cells with HbF stay pink.","Not its purpose.","Weak D is tested with IAT.","That is antibody identification."]'::jsonb, 2, 'verified'
