select null, t.id, 'builtin', 'The classical complement pathway begins when which component binds to antigen-antibody complexes?', '["C3","C1q","Factor B","Mannose-binding lectin"]'::jsonb, 1, 'IgG or IgM bound to an antigen recruits and activates the C1 complex (through C1q), starting the classical pathway. Reference: OpenStax Microbiology, 18.1 Overview of Specific Adaptive Immunity (openstax.org/books/microbiology/pages/18-1-overview-of-specific-adaptive-immunity); Berentsen, Cold agglutinin disease, Hematology Am Soc Hematol Educ Program 2016 (pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6142439).', '["Part of all pathways, but not the starting component.","Binds antibody Fc and starts the classical pathway.","Part of the alternative pathway.","Starts the lectin pathway."]'::jsonb, 2, 'verified'
